# The version of this repository, and of everything `aowl release` produces
# from it. One line, no syntax. The first line that is neither blank nor a
# comment is the version; nothing else here is parsed.
#
# What it means: the bundle. Every appearance of it elsewhere is derived and
# none of them is typed a second time --
#
#   aowlspt-<v>-<date>.zip        the archive's name
#   aowlspt-<v>/VERSION           a copy of this file, inside it
#   aowlspt-<v>/payload/payload.json   its "version", patched in as the archive
#                                 is built, so the installer reads it
#   <target>\aowlspt-install.txt  written there by `aowlspt-install` from that
#                                 field, so a finished install can still say
#                                 which build it is
#   MANIFEST.sha256, CHANGELOG.md their headings
#
# What it is not: a Tarkov version (that is `targetTarkovVersion` in
# payload.json, and it moves when the game does), and not a mod version (those
# are in registry/mods.json and move independently).
#
# The working copy of installer/payload/payload.json is per-machine and
# .gitignore'd, so its "version" drifts. `aowl release` says so and overrides
# it; an install made straight out of installer/payload will report whatever
# that file said, which is one of the ways to tell a development install from
# a released one.
